{"availability":"available","full":"Supreet37/Mega_Project","name":"Mega_Project","description":"A fully responsive learning and internship platform built using React, Vite, and Tailwind CSS. It enables students to explore and enroll in programming courses, submit feedback, participate in events and hackathons.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":3,"forks":1,"created":"2025-07-02T02:52:08Z","updated":"2026-06-08T05:58:22Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://code-bridgeeducation.netlify.app/","topics":["backend","demo","educational-project","frontend","js","localhost","react"],"demo":"https://code-bridgeeducation.netlify.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:58.751Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:58.751Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T05:07:58.751Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T05:07:58.751Z","stars":3,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["CodeBridge is a fully responsive learning and internship platform built using React, Vite, and Tailwind CSS. It enables students to explore and enroll in programming courses, submit feedback, participate in events and hackathons.","CodeBridge supports two user flows: Students and Administrators. Students can enroll in coding courses using a cart system, submit testimonials, and explore hackathons/events. The administrator view allows posting events and managing content. Built with Tailwind CSS, the design is desktop-first, scalable, and interactive.","This project demonstrates a complete frontend workflow using React Hooks, React Router, Axios for API communication, and JSON Server for local backend simulation."],"features":["👤 Separate interfaces for Students and Admins","📚 Browse, enroll, and manage coding courses","🛒 Slide-down Cart with dynamic item counter","📝 Feedback form connected to Testimonials using Axios (POST & GET)","🎯 Hackathon/Event posting panel for admins"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Supreet37/Mega_